*> PLB-C042 inspect-count-not-reset: INSPECT TALLYING adds to its
*> count, which the paragraph, or one leading into it, should reset:
*> COUNT-INIT resets WS-BLANKS and falls into COUNT-TEST.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. TALLIES.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-FLAGS            PIC X(7) VALUE "SU SU S".
01  WS-COUNTS.
    05  WS-SELECTED     PIC 9(3).
    05  WS-BLANKS       PIC 9(3).
01  I                   PIC 9(3).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 7
        DISPLAY WS-FLAGS(I:1)
    END-PERFORM
    PERFORM COUNT-RESET
    PERFORM COUNT-GROUP-RESET
    PERFORM COUNT-NOT-RESET
    GO TO COUNT-INIT.
COUNT-RESET.
    MOVE ZERO TO WS-SELECTED
    INSPECT WS-FLAGS TALLYING WS-SELECTED FOR ALL "S".
COUNT-GROUP-RESET.
    INITIALIZE WS-COUNTS
    INSPECT WS-FLAGS TALLYING WS-SELECTED FOR ALL "S"
                              WS-BLANKS FOR ALL SPACES.
COUNT-NOT-RESET.
    INSPECT WS-FLAGS TALLYING I FOR ALL "U"
    DISPLAY I WS-SELECTED WS-BLANKS.
COUNT-INIT.
    MOVE ZERO TO WS-BLANKS.
COUNT-TEST.
    INSPECT WS-FLAGS TALLYING WS-BLANKS FOR ALL SPACES
    DISPLAY WS-BLANKS
    STOP RUN.
